# ###########################################################################
# NOT A FIXTURE PATH � retained as the address-verification harness only.
# Parked FR/LG saves are supplied by hand, not played from a new game
# (DECISIONS.md ADR-0022).  No test script references this file.  It is kept
# because running it is how the "D" (verified live) rows of the FR/LG table
# in docs/AUTOPILOT.md were observed, and the chain deliberately stops one
# leg short of a wireless counter.  See that document's "Empirical-
# verification harness" section before touching it.
# ###########################################################################
# firered_newgame.inputs — Phase-4 FR/LG fixture generation, FIRERED side.
#
# Plays a BRAND NEW GAME (no save) to the Viridian City Pokemon Center 2F
# Union Room counter with two party mons, and in-game saves there.  The
# LeafGreen twin is leafgreen_newgame.inputs; the two differ only in the
# typed trainer name and the starter taken (distinct trainer identities —
# identical trainers in a Union Room are an untested edge case).
#
# Target: Pokemon FireRed USA (BPRE **rev 1**, DECISIONS.md ADR-0009).
# Addresses: docs/AUTOPILOT.md "FR/LG (BPRE/BPGE rev 1)" table.  Function
# pointer compares carry the Thumb bit.
#   gMain.callback2       0x030030F4  (gMain 0x030030F0 + 4)
#   CB2_TitleScreenRun    0x08078BB1   CB2_MainMenu   0x0800C2E9
#   CB2_NamingScreen      0x0809FB85   CB2_Overworld  0x080565C9
#   BattleMainCB2         0x08011115
#   gSaveBlock1Ptr        0x03005008   (+0x00 pos, +0x04 WarpData)
#   gObjectEvents[0].currentCoords  x 0x02036E48  y 0x02036E4A (+7 MAP_OFFSET)
#   gPlayerPartyCount     0x02024029   gPlayerParty   0x02024284
#   sStartMenuCursorPos   0x020370F4   sNumStartMenuItems 0x020370F5
#   sSaveDialogCB         0x03000FA4   (IWRAM — Emerald's is EWRAM)
#   SaveDialogCB_ReturnSuccess 0x0806F9F5
# map loc u16 (mapGroup | mapNum<<8), from pret data/maps/map_groups.json:
#   house2F 0x0104  house1F 0x0004  PalletTown 0x0003  OaksLab 0x0304
#   Route1 0x1303  ViridianCity 0x0103  ViridianMart 0x0305
#   PC1F 0x0405  PC2F 0x0505  UnionRoom 0x0400
#
# Route (why it is this long): the Union Room attendant is gated on
# FLAG_SYS_POKEDEX_GET (pret data/scripts/cable_club.inc
# CableClub_EventScript_UnionRoomAttendant) and on CountPartyNonEggMons >= 2
# (CableClub_EventScript_CheckPartyUnionRoomRequirements), so the fixture
# must complete the Oak's-Parcel round trip AND catch a second mon.  The
# earliest Poke Balls in the game are the five Oak hands over with the
# Pokedex (PalletTown_ProfessorOaksLab/scripts.inc:660), so the order is
# forced: starter -> Viridian Mart (parcel) -> Oak (Pokedex + balls) ->
# Route 1 grass (catch) -> Viridian PC 2F.
#
# Walking idiom: Route 1 is tall grass on every through-route, so a wild
# battle can start at any step.  Each leg is
#     repeat N { wait 30 ; mash A until CB2_Overworld ; press DIR }
# — the "mash A until CB2_Overworld" is a no-op in the field (the predicate
# already holds, so no button is pressed) and a battle-resolver otherwise,
# and it runs BEFORE the next D-pad press so no D-pad input ever reaches the
# battle action menu (gActionSelectionCursor persists across turns; a stray
# DOWN would leave the cursor on POKEMON and the next A would open the party
# menu).  A reverse-direction holdmash then lands the exact tile.
ff on

# ============================================================================
# 1. Intro: title -> NEW GAME -> Oak's speech -> naming -> bedroom
# ============================================================================
mash A 4 0x030030F4 0xFFFFFFFF 0x08078BB1 14400
evt title_ok

# Everything from NEW GAME to the player naming screen is A-mashable
# (controls guide 3 pages, Pikachu intro 3 pages, Oak speech, BOY on row 0
# of the no-wrap gender menu).
mash A 4 0x030030F4 0xFFFFFFFF 0x0809FB85 36000
evt naming_player
dump

# FR/LG has NO preset list for the PLAYER name (pret src/oak_speech.c
# Task_OakSpeech_DoNamingScreen goes straight to DoNamingScreen) — type on
# the keyboard.  Cursor starts at (0,0)='A'; page rows are
#   A B C D E F _ .   /  G H I J K L _ ,  /  M N O P Q R S  /  T U V W X Y Z
# START jumps the cursor to OK (naming_screen.c MoveCursorToOKButton).
# FireRed types "FR": F=(5,0), R=(5,2).
repeat 5
press RIGHT 4
wait 6
endrepeat
press A 4
wait 10
press DOWN 4
wait 6
press DOWN 4
wait 6
press A 4
wait 10
press START 4
wait 20
press A 4
wait 20
waitramne 4 0x030030F4 0xFFFFFFFF 0x0809FB85 900
evt naming_player_done

# rival name: the rival DOES get a preset list, but row 0 is NEW NAME and A
# takes it, so the keyboard appears again — type one char and confirm.
mash A 4 0x030030F4 0xFFFFFFFF 0x0809FB85 36000
evt naming_rival
repeat 3
press A 4
wait 8
endrepeat
press START 4
wait 20
press A 4
wait 20
waitramne 4 0x030030F4 0xFFFFFFFF 0x0809FB85 900

mash A 4 0x030030F4 0xFFFFFFFF 0x080565C9 36000
evt overworld_ok
wait 120
logptr loc_bedroom 2 0x03005008 0x04

# ============================================================================
# 2. Bedroom -> Pallet Town
# ============================================================================
# FR/LG house stairs are DIRECTIONAL stair warps: the 2F tile (10,2) is
# MB_DOWN_LEFT_STAIR_WARP (0x6F) and IsDirectionalStairWarpMetatileBehavior
# only fires for DIR_WEST, so walking up ONTO it does nothing (confirmed
# live: standing on (10,2) never warped).  Arrive moving left.
holdmash RIGHT B 2 0x02036E48 0xFFFF 18 900
holdmash LEFT B 2 0x02036E48 0xFFFF 18 300
holdmash UP B 2 0x02036E4A 0xFFFF 9 900
holdmash DOWN B 2 0x02036E4A 0xFFFF 9 300
holdmashptr LEFT B 2 0x03005008 0x04 0xFFFF 0x0004 900
evt house1f_ok
wait 60

# 1F (10,2) -> row 8 -> doormat (4,8), which is MB_SOUTH_ARROW_WARP: it
# fires on a southward step, so hold DOWN through it.
holdmash DOWN B 2 0x02036E4A 0xFFFF 15 900
holdmash UP B 2 0x02036E4A 0xFFFF 15 300
holdmash LEFT B 2 0x02036E48 0xFFFF 11 900
holdmash RIGHT B 2 0x02036E48 0xFFFF 11 300
holdmashptr DOWN B 2 0x03005008 0x04 0xFFFF 0x0003 900
evt pallet_ok
wait 60

# ============================================================================
# 3. Pallet Town -> Oak's lab (forced), starter, rival battle
# ============================================================================
# The coord trigger at (12,1)/(13,1) fires while VAR_MAP_SCENE_PALLET_TOWN_OAK
# == 0; Oak walks the player into the lab and the script ends in
# `warp MAP_PALLET_TOWN_PROFESSOR_OAKS_LAB, 6, 12`.
holdmash RIGHT B 2 0x02036E48 0xFFFF 19 900
holdmash LEFT B 2 0x02036E48 0xFFFF 19 300
holdmash UP B 2 0x02036E4A 0xFFFF 8 900
evt oak_trigger
mashptr A 2 0x03005008 0x04 0xFFFF 0x0304 10800
evt oakslab_ok

# ChooseStarterScene walks the player (6,12) -> (6,4); its remaining msgboxes
# are still running when the player lands, and the B pulses clear them.
mash A 4 0x02036E4A 0xFFFF 11 10800
evt starter_scene_done
wait 60

# Balls are objects at (8,4) Bulbasaur / (9,4) Squirtle / (10,4) Charmander;
# row 4 is blocked by them, so approach along row 5 and face north.
# FireRed takes SQUIRTLE (9,4) -> stand (9,5) = obj x 16.
holdmash DOWN B 2 0x02036E4A 0xFFFF 13 5400
holdmash RIGHT B 2 0x02036E48 0xFFFF 16 900
holdmash LEFT B 2 0x02036E48 0xFFFF 16 300
wait 40
press UP 2
wait 30
press UP 2
wait 30
mash A 1 0x02024029 0xFF 1 5400
evt got_starter
logram pers0 4 0x02024284

# "Give it a nickname?" is answered NO by the B pulses below.  The rival
# parks beside the table so row 5 is not usable westbound — drop to row 6.
holdmash DOWN B 2 0x02036E4A 0xFFFF 13 5400
holdmash LEFT B 2 0x02036E48 0xFFFF 13 3600
holdmash RIGHT B 2 0x02036E48 0xFFFF 13 600
holdmash DOWN B 2 0x02036E4A 0xFFFF 15 3600
evt at_rival_trigger
# the trigger's intro msgbox needs presses before the battle starts, so mash
# INTO BattleMainCB2 rather than waiting on it.  The battle is unfailable:
# TRAINER_BATTLE_EARLY_RIVAL heals and returns to the field either way.
mash A 4 0x030030F4 0xFFFFFFFF 0x08011115 7200
evt battle_start
mash A 4 0x030030F4 0xFFFFFFFF 0x080565C9 54000
evt battle_done
wait 120

# ============================================================================

# ============================================================================
# 5. Leave the lab and in-game SAVE (stage boundary)
# ============================================================================
# The post-battle scene (Oak's speech, the rival leaving) is still running
# when CB2_Overworld returns, so the player is locked; the B pulses of the
# walk south clear it before the hold takes effect.
holdmash DOWN B 2 0x02036E4A 0xFFFF 18 18000
holdmashptr DOWN B 2 0x03005008 0x04 0xFFFF 0x0003 3600
evt pallet_exit
wait 120
holdmash DOWN B 2 0x02036E4A 0xFFFF 21 900
wait 60

# The autopilot engine caps a script at 256 steps
# (frontend-common/fe_autopilot.c AP_MAX_STEPS � not ours to change) and the
# full FR/LG new-game route is several times that, so the route is split into
# four stages chained through the .sav file, exactly the way the Emerald
# fixtures chain emerald_park.inputs into the trade scripts.
# Start menu here (FLAG_SYS_POKEMON_GET set, no Pokedex yet):
#   POKEMON BAG PLAYER SAVE OPTION EXIT  -> 6 items, SAVE at index 3.
press START 4
wait 60
waitram 1 0x020370F5 0xFF 6 900
repeat 3
press DOWN 4
wait 12
endrepeat
waitram 1 0x020370F4 0xFF 3 300
press A 4
waitramne 4 0x03000FA4 0xFFFFFFFF 0x00000000 900
mashsram A 5400
evt sram_written
mash A 4 0x03000FA4 0xFFFFFFFF 0x0806F9F5 3600
wait 300
press START 4
wait 60
press B 4
wait 60
logptr end_loc 2 0x03005008 0x04
logram end_x 2 0x02036E48
logram end_y 2 0x02036E4A
logram party_count 1 0x02024029
dump
evt stage1_done
